    "title": "Major Mobile street closed for water leak repair - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Michael Hanich ,\n1 hours ago\nVideo above: ‘News 5 Now’ — Top Stories from Sept. 16, 2026\nMOBILE, Ala. (WKRG) — A major road in Mobile will be closed on Thursday for city officials to repair a water leak.\nArgument over missing dog ends in deadly baseball bat attack in Thomasville According to a Facebook post from the City of Mobile Animal Service s , Virginia Street from Ann Street to Broad Street will be closed on Thursday, Sept. 17, for city crews to repair a water leak. The post said commuters cannot access the City of Mobile Animal Services facility from Virginia Street.\nOfficials said there are two alternate routes available: Broad Street to Baltimore Street to Kelly Street to Owens Street, or Ann Street to Baltimore Street to Kelly Street to Owens Street to reach Animal Services.\nThe post said the repairs may take a few days, but should be completed by the end of Saturday, Sept. 19.\nFlorida State, LSU softball set for fall showdown in Orange Beach Animal Services will remain open every weekday from 10 a.m. to 4 p.m. during this road work.\nCopyright 2026 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed.\nFor the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to WKRG News 5.",
    "summary": "Video above: ‘News 5 Now’ — Top Stories from Sept. 16, 2026 MOBILE, Ala. (WKRG) — A major road in Mobile will be closed on Thursday for city officials to repair a water leak. Argument over missing dog ends in deadly baseball bat attack in Thomasville According to a Facebook post from the City of Mobile Animal Service s , Virginia Street from Ann Street to Broad Street will be closed on Thursday, Sept. 17, for city crews to repair a water leak. The post said commuters cannot access the City of Mobile Animal Services facility from Virginia Street.",
